Wayland: frameless floating dock containers that dock by their title bar

A floating container on Wayland gets a compositor decoration. Dragging it only
moves the window - the client never learns about the move - so the widget
cannot be docked back by dragging its title bar, and the dock area title bar
below it, which can, looks like a second, redundant title bar.

Make the floating container frameless instead, so the dock area title bar is
its only title bar: dragging it moves the window (xdg_toplevel_drag_v1) and
docks it on a drop indicator. It gets the close button, and a double click
maximizes. A thin border around the content resizes the window via
QWindow::startSystemResize() and outlines it.

Also make the dock manager window the transient parent of floating containers,
so the compositor keeps them above the main window as on other platforms.

Applied to Qt Advanced Docking System v5.1.1 by FetchContent (CMakeLists.txt).

